I just had a second YASD that I can recall on the castle level - I let
myself get engulfed by an air elemental while weak then, yes, I passed
out - after I had cleared the level.  (On the other one, I was kicking
a stack of equipment down the hall while waiting for a horde of
something to reach me, and nailed a chickatrice corpse.)

The biggest downer, apart from the death itself, was the fact that I
wasted what would have been a nice bones file.  (Or, being a Hearse
user, I wasted the chance to donate a nice file and potentially get a
new interesting one in return.)

So I got to wondering - what is the reason that some levels aren't
eligible for bones?  Is it a technical issue?  Game balance?
Something else?

Looking at the bones spoiler, it looks like most ineligible levels
are branches or special levels.  DL1-3 I can understand, that's too
early for a demon lord or ascension kit.

But I don't see how there could be a balance issue with the branch
levels.  Without diving into the code, it doesn't seem like it would
be difficult to call up (for example) a mines branch bones when a
player gets to the appropriate level, and send each stair to a branch.

But then, I also understand that the source code isn't always
straightforward either.

The special levels could be a balance issue, I suppose.  It would
certainly suck if Sokoban was unpassable, or worse, if the /oW was
gone from the castle.  But I'd be willing to sacrifice an occasional
luckstone for the chance at an interesting bones on Medusa.  Would it
be too easy if the castle was cleared and the /oW was just on the
statue of some idiot who kicked a chickatrice corpse?  Maybe, but no
easier than if someone with a /oW had done the same thing on the
previous level.  Some levels have items needed for ascension, maybe
those need to be no-bones; or maybe the required item (and the monster
guarding it) could just be added if they aren't already on the level.

Anyway, I was just wondering if any source divers could give a
technical reason, or if I'm underestimating the balance issues.  I
didn't mean to launch into a long rant...



